    "url": "https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/alan/61881e0e-6149-4e0a-9a24-5ac1a315d411",
    "source": "ashby:alan",
    "_descr": "HEALTH CAN’T WAIT. \n\nNot for symptoms to get worse. Not for a six‑month appointment. Not for a system to catch up. But that’s exactly how healthcare works today. You wait, until you can’t.\n\nAlan exists to end the wait.\n\nHealth is a universal right, and we believe this right can only become real when it’s coupled with prevention. We need to stop treating health as something we repair and start treating it as something we build, every day. It’s not solely a question of willpower. It’s the healthcare system itself that needs to work for everyone, in a sustainable way.\n\nSo we are building the new standard in prevention insurance. Alan is the first company that integrates insurance, prevention, and care into a single, acclaimed user experience.\n\nWe are on an incredible journey to build a global leading company, with a unique culture https://alan.com/en/careers. We already partner with 40K+ companies of all sizes, serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.\n\nPrevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 800+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.\n\n\n⭐️ THE INTERNAL CONTROL ROLE ⭐️\n\nAlan's Corporate team brings together Risk, Corporate Governance, Internal Control, Legal, Compliance and Security around a shared mission: building the infrastructure that lets Alan operate at scale, safely and responsibly. Internal Control helps design, implement and monitor controls within the business so operations run in line with members' interests, the strategy, our objectives and the law.\n\n\n\nWe are looking for a high-potential internal control professional who can define and own control activities end-to-end, and grow into ownership of more complex control scopes over time.\n\n\n\nThis is not a traditional, box-checking control role. We build solutions and act as genuine business partners on risks. This is an opportunity to be part of the next generation of risk professionals: developing automated controls, documentation and using AI to detect emerging risks early.\n\n\n\n\n⭐️ YOUR MISSIONS ⭐️\n\n - Internal Control\n   \n   - You will define and implement control frameworks on processes, leveraging Alan’s culture of transparency and distributed ownership, and pushing for reliability and scalability: AI and automation, smart processes\n   \n   - You will help strengthening our system for identifying and monitoring risks and co-build the next generation of risk tooling\n   \n   - You will perform second-level reviews on high-risk areas\n   \n   - You will drive efforts to ensure proper controls documentation and communicability to third parties partners\n   \n   - You will support the management of audits from commercial partners and supervisors\n\n - Team growth\n   \n   - You will help expand risk management reflexes throughout the company, and assist teams such as Insurance, Operations, Security and Legal to design and implement action plans to mitigate our risks\n   \n   - You will create resources to raise awareness and empower the team for risk management, internal control and regulatory compliance;\n   \n   - You will support the identification and hiring of new talents for the team.\n     \n     \n\n\n⭐️ IS IT WHAT YOU ARE LOOKING FOR? ⭐️\n\nYou may be a great fit if you have:\n\n - At least two years of experience in internal control or a risk function - in insurance, a Big Four, or a regulated / fast-growing environment\n\n - Fluent in both French and English\n\n - A solid understanding of Solvency II and domain expertise (e.g. insurance operations, reserving, underwriting, reporting frameworks)\n\n - Comfort with AI and automation tools to scale controls, as well as anticipation of how AI reshapes controls\n\n - A builder's mindset: you're excited to build something differentiated, you don't thrive solely on established processes\n\n - A business-partner attitude: you act as a true partner to product teams, helping solve their control issues and risks rather than acting only as a controller\n\n - A written-first and rigorous working style: you’re structured, precise and at ease with Alan's async communication culture\n   \n   \n\nAs a plus:\n\n - Multi-jurisdiction exposure (France, Belgium, Spain, Canada/OSFI)\n\n - Exposure to the DORA framework\n\n - Exposure to HDS and ISO 27001\n   \n   \n\nFor this role, we are looking to hire within the C0 to C1 level range https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity.\n\n\n\n\n🌍 HOW WE WORK\n\nLocation: You must be legally eligible to work from France. Role will preferably be based in Paris.\n\nRemote work: We offer remote work flexibility, but we value in-person collaboration\n\n\n\n\n🎯 IMPORTANT NOTE: WE HIRE PEOPLE, NOT ROLES.\n\nIf you're excited about this opportunity but don't check every box, we'd love to hear from you. Everyone, no matter how underrepresented, should feel free to apply, as it can only bring learnings or success.\n\n\n\nIf you identify yourself as a woman: Did you know that research shows women often apply only when meeting 100% of requirements?\n\n\n\nRemember, this is just a guide, not a checklist. We'll be thrilled to receive your application!\n\n\n\n🔖 Check out our About Alan https://alan.com/about and Career https://alan.com/careers pages, as well as our Medium https://medium.com/alan, blog https://blog.alan.com/ and Glassdoor page https://www.glassdoor.com/Overview/Working-at-Alan-EI_IE1696043.11,15.htm for more info.\n\n\n\n\nYOU WANT TO KNOW MORE ABOUT ALAN?\n\n🙌 Perks & Benefits https://alan.com/en/careers/a/salary-equity: Alaners are provided with a stimulating environment and perks ensuring they are happy, efficient and spend only high-quality time with co-workers.\n\n🤘A strong culture https://alan.com/en/about/a/leadership-principles: People joining Alan are often surprised and delighted by our innovative working method. We have a set of cultural values that guide our approach to work",
